   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to an\nexemption for certain property from the prohibition of alcohol sales within a\ncertain distance of a church",
    "basePrintNo": "S6665",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6665-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6665\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to an\nexemption for certain property from the prohibition of alcohol sales\nwithin a certain distance of a church\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide an exemption from the Alcoholic Beverage Control Law, enabl-\ning an establishment within the City of Hudson located within two-hun-\ndred feet of a church to be eligible to apply for a liquor license from\nthe NYS Liquor Authority.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 7 of Section 64 of the Alcoholic Beverage\nControl Law by adding a new paragraph (e-17) allowing an establishment\nwithin the City of Hudson located within two-hundred feet of a church,\nsynagogue, or other place, of worship to be eligible to apply for a\nliquor license from the NYS Liquor Authority.\n\n§ 2: Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will allow the establishment located at 402 Warren Street\nHudson, NY to apply for a liquor license from the New York State Author-\nity despite being within 200 feet of First Presbyterian Church.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
